{"v":3,"src":"MOV     AH, 47h          ; DOS: the current directory of drive DL\nMOV     DL, 0            ; 0 = the current drive, 1 = A\nMOV     SI, OFFSET PATH1 ; DS:SI = 64 bytes for the path\nINT     21h\nMOV     AH, 19h          ; 47h leaves out the drive: print it first\nINT     21h\nADD     AL, \"A\"\nMOV     DL, AL\nMOV     AH, 02h\nINT     21h\nMOV     DL, \":\"\nMOV     AH, 02h\nINT     21h\nMOV     DL, \"\\\"          ; and the backslash after it\nMOV     AH, 02h\nINT     21h\nCLD\nMOV     SI, OFFSET PATH1\nNEXT1:\nLODSB                    ; the path ends with a 0 byte\nOR      AL, AL\nJZ      DONE1\nMOV     DL, AL\nMOV     AH, 02h\nINT     21h\nJMP     NEXT1\nDONE1:\nMOV     DX, OFFSET CRLF\nMOV     AH, 09h\nINT     21h\nMOV     DX, OFFSET BADM1\nMOV     AH, 09h\nINT     21h\nMOV     AH, 47h          ; a drive that cannot exist\nMOV     DL, 27\nMOV     SI, OFFSET PATH1\nINT     21h\nCALL    RESULT           ; error 15: invalid drive\n\nPATH1   DB      64 DUP(0)\nBADM1   DB      \"drive 27: $\"\nRESULT  PROC    NEAR     ; print \"ok\", or \"error\" and AX when CF = 1\nPUSHF                    ; keeps AX and CF for the caller\nPUSH    AX\nMOV     DX, OFFSET OKMSG\nJNC     RESULT1\nMOV     DX, OFFSET ERRMSG\nMOV     AH, 09h\nINT     21h\nPOP     AX\nPUSH    AX\nCALL    PDEC             ; the error code\nMOV     DX, OFFSET CRLF\nRESULT1:\nMOV     AH, 09h\nINT     21h\nPOP     AX\nPOPF\nRET\nRESULT  ENDP\nOKMSG   DB      \"ok\", 13, 10, \"$\"\nERRMSG  DB      \"error $\"\nPDEC    PROC    NEAR     ; print AX in decimal (changes AX BX CX DX)\nMOV     BX, 10\nXOR     CX, CX           ; digits on the stack\nPDEC1:\nXOR     DX, DX\nDIV     BX               ; AX = AX / 10, DX = the last digit\nPUSH    DX\nINC     CX\nOR      AX, AX\nJNZ     PDEC1\nPDEC2:\nPOP     DX               ; the digits come back first to last\nADD     DL, \"0\"\nMOV     AH, 02h\nINT     21h\nLOOP    PDEC2\nRET\nPDEC    ENDP\nCRLF    DB      13, 10, \"$\"","seg":2070,"dataAt":401,"vars":[{"na